    "address": "2322 Broadway, New York, NY 10024",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nLocated squarely on the vibrant Upper West Side, this upscale American eatery is anchored beautifully at 2322 Broadway, sitting proudly between 84th and 85th Streets.\n\nThe Jacob’s Pedigree\nThis magnificent establishment is the highly acclaimed, sophisticated sister restaurant to the legendary Jacob’s Pickles, elevating classic American comfort food with a stunning, French-inspired culinary twist.\n\nThe French Dip Architecture\nYou absolutely must order their signature French Dip. The culinary team masterfully stacks mountains of incredibly tender, slow-roasted beef on artisanal French bread, served alongside a brilliant, deeply savory cup of hot au jus.\n\nThe Gruyère Crown\nElevate the classic sandwich by ordering the Deluxe version. It features a flawless, bubbling crown of rich, heavily melted Gruyère cheese and deeply caramelized onions baked directly onto the hot crust.\n\nThe Brioche Masterpiece\nDo not skip the appetizers. Their legendary pull-apart bread is a towering, beautifully baked brioche masterpiece, glistening with rich garlic butter and meant to be aggressively torn apart by hand.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered sandwiches carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly engineered to effortlessly fuel a massive day of exploring the expansive museums and historic streets of the surrounding neighborhood.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously monumental, beautifully split a French Dip and an order of the rich pull-apart bread with a travel companion to sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit without feeling weighed down.\n\nThe Vintage Aesthetic\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously designed interior. It features soaring ceilings, deeply tufted green leather booths, and warm, glowing vintage chandeliers that evoke the timeless elegance of classic New York dining.\n\nThe Bar Architecture\nThe massive, sweeping bar is an absolute design triumph. Backlit shelves brilliantly showcase an incredible library of premium spirits, framed perfectly by classic subway tiles and highly polished dark wood accents.\n\nThe Cocktail Presentation\nThe mixology program here is an absolute masterclass. Their signature cocktails are presented in stunning, heavy-bottomed crystal glassware, brilliantly garnished with fresh herbs and large, perfectly clear artisanal ice cubes.\n\nThe Macro Perspective\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the French Dip to beautifully capture the glistening, savory juices of the slow-roasted beef and the heavy, shining cheese pull.\n\nThe Au Jus Action\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the heavy, rich au jus cascading directly over the toasted bread and tender beef as you dunk the sandwich.\n\nThe Tungsten Glow\nThe restaurant is bathed in beautifully warm, low-level tungsten lighting. Lean into this classic, moody atmosphere by resting your camera on the table to capture the brilliant reflections off the crystal glassware without ever using a harsh flash.\n\nThe Central Park Pivot\nOnce you finish your incredibly satisfying meal, take a scenic walk to burn off the rich food. Head exactly three blocks east to seamlessly transition into the sweeping, beautifully landscaped, historic paths of Central Park.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nTransit is incredibly effortless. Take the 1 train directly to the 86th Street station. Emerge from the underground and enjoy a beautiful, incredibly short two-block walk south down the vibrant Broadway corridor to hit the stunning storefront.",
