    "address": "2571 Hempstead Tpke Ste 100, East Meadow, NY 11554",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This massive, bustling cathedral of American steakhouse culture is anchored beautifully at 280 Marsh Avenue, sitting perfectly within the sprawling retail complex of the Staten Island Mall.\n\nThe Architectural Scale\nThis is not a cramped Manhattan dining room. The building is a massive, sprawling, brilliantly constructed wooden lodge featuring soaring ceilings, bright neon accents, and a classic footprint that perfectly captures the expansive spirit of the American West.\n\nThe Meat Display\nStep inside the front doors and admire the stunning, brightly lit glass meat cooler. The culinary team meticulously displays the hand-cut, brilliantly marbled steaks like precious artifacts, perfectly showcasing the incredible quality of the beef before it hits the roaring grill.\n\nThe Cinnamon Butter Foundation\nDo not ignore the complimentary bread basket. It arrives to the table as a towering, beautifully baked foundation of fresh, warm yeast rolls, served alongside a flawless, deeply sweet, and perfectly whipped cinnamon butter.\n\nThe Bone-In Ribeye\nYou absolutely must order their signature bone-in ribeye. The culinary team masterfully sears this massive, beautifully marbled cut over an open flame to create a flawless, caramelized crust while locking in the rich, deeply savory juices.\n\nThe Cactus Blossom\nThe appetizers are absolute architectural marvels. The legendary Cactus Blossom is a towering, flawlessly deep-fried colossus of a sweet onion, brilliantly engineered to pull apart into perfect, golden, crispy petals ready for dunking in their rich, signature sauce.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously colossal, beautifully split a massive steak and a towering mountain of loaded potato skins with a travel companion. This allows you to seamlessly sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit without ordering excess.\n\nThe Line Dancing Theater\nVisit during the peak dinner rush to witness a masterclass in dining entertainment. The incredibly energetic, beautifully choreographed speed of the waitstaff breaking into spontaneous line dances is a brilliant, highly spirited display of unique restaurant culture.\n\nThe Peanut Tradition\nEmbrace the absolute classic, nostalgic energy of the dining room. The experience is beautifully defined by the legendary buckets of complimentary roasted peanuts on the tables, creating an incredibly relaxed, welcoming, and uniquely interactive atmosphere.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered American dishes carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly designed to effortlessly fuel a massive evening of exploring the expansive retail avenues of the surrounding Staten Island landscape.\n\nThe Ice-Cold Tap\nThe beverage program is an absolute triumph of temperature control. Their signature draft beers and margaritas are served in brilliantly frosted, heavy glass mugs, ensuring a flawless, refreshing, ice-cold sip that perfectly cuts through the rich, savory steaks.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the towering ribeye to beautifully capture the glistening, savory juices, the perfect crosshatch grill marks, and the melting pat of seasoned butter.\n\nThe Action Shot\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the waitstaff setting down the massive, steaming plates, perfectly highlighting the incredible, generous scale of the beautifully plated meal.\n\nThe Retail Pivot\nOnce you finish your incredibly satisfying meal, you are standing directly at the heart of the island's premier shopping destination. Walk exactly a few steps to seamlessly transition into the sweeping, brilliantly illuminated concourses of the Staten Island Mall.\n\nThe Transit Approach\nTransit is an incredible, scenic journey. Take the iconic, absolutely beautiful and free Staten Island Ferry across the glittering New York Harbor, then effortlessly board the S44 or S94 bus directly to the mall concourse for a seamless, brilliant arrival.",
